3. Heard Mr. D.P. Dhal, learned Senior Counsel for the appellants and Ms. Sarita Moharana, learned Additional Standing Counsel for the State.
4. The prosecution, in order to bring home the charges, examined as many as eleven witnesses, Out of whom, P.Ws. 1, 3, 5 and 7 were the witnesses to the inquest, P.Ws.2, 3, 4, 5 and 6 were the witnesses to the Panch that was convened in the maternal house of the deceased before her death;
P.W.8 was the witness to the seizure; P.W.9 was the witness to the consumption of poison by the deceased.
